  "notes": "Cause code left TBD/provisional per FORM-366 fields; root cause undetermined due to internal breaker damage destroying evidence. Modeled the fire and the battery ground condition as parallel/downstream failure modes both stemming from the AVR feedback thermal-runaway loop, since narrative frames them as distinct effects (fire from heat; battery ground discovered later, traced to control power sharing with AVR/exciter). RCIC and HPCS explicitly auto-started per design and used operationally to control level during the event -> modeled as BACKED_UP_BY. No EIIS codes given for RCIC/HPCS in narrative (only names), left null per rule 2. No previous similar LER referenced (Section V.B states 'None') so no stub LER/SIMILAR_TO edge emitted. Plant/unit/reactor type/vendor inferred from title and docket (NMP2 = Nine Mile Point Unit 2, BWR, GE) since FORM-366 fields left them null."
